<title>LEBANON: Lebanon issues money supply statistics.</title>
<headline>Lebanon issues money supply statistics.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lebanon released on Tuesday latest statistics on money supply during the month of December (blns of Lebanese pounds at end of period):</p>
<p>				  M1	   M2	 M3	M4</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    Nov			1693	13572     28313   32790</p>
<p>    Dec			1753	14002     29241   33708</p>
<p>1995</p>
<p>    Dec			1561	 9663     22883   26233</p>
<p>1994</p>
<p>    Dec			1437	 8587     19651   21549</p>
<p>1993</p>
<p>    Dec			1143	 5309     15678    N/A</p>
<p>The Bank defined the aggregates as follows:</p>
<p>M1 -- Currency in circulation + Demand deposits</p>
<p>M2 -- M1 + Other deposits in Lebanese pounds</p>
<p>M3 -- M2 + Deposits in F.X.</p>
<p>M4 -- M3 + Treasury bills held by the non-banking system</p>
<p>($1 = 1,556 Lebanese pounds in October)</p>
</text>
